THROWAWAY SCAFFOLDING. Delete this patch, do not maintain it.

Let the Dart lifecycle guard heal a thread-token mismatch instead of throwing.

Upstream #399 added `NativeHandleState._checkOwnerIsolate`, which compares the
native thread token and throws `wrongThread`. That is a deliberate change and a
good one: it turns silent corruption into a loud error and names its issue,
maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi#412. This patch disables it, and is therefore not
upstreamable and must never be offered as one.

Why we carry it anyway: our engine drives the map from a spawned Dart isolate,
and the VM moves that isolate between OS threads (7 distinct threads observed in
a single 60-second session on a Xiaomi 2109119DG). Patch 0002 handles that with
`mln_runtime_rebind_thread`, but `RuntimeHandle.rebindThread()` reads `_pointer`,
which goes through the new guard, so the rebind is gated by the very check it
exists to clear. At pin 9d1508dc the engine isolate throws and dies a few
seconds after the map opens.

What it does:

  * `NativeHandleState._ownerThreadToken` becomes mutable.
  * On a thread-token mismatch, `_checkOwnerIsolate` calls an installed rebind
    and refreshes its own token instead of throwing. The rebind is process-wide
    and idempotent, so handles heal independently on their next use, in any
    order, and no registry of handles is needed.
  * `RuntimeHandle` installs that rebind, because it is the only handle that can
    reach `mln_runtime_rebind_thread`. It reads its address without owner
    validation, since going through `_pointer` would re-enter the guard.
  * The isolate-hash branch is untouched and still throws. A genuinely different
    isolate is a real error and stays loud; only the thread-token branch heals.

The hook is per-isolate rather than per-handle because `MapProjectionHandle` and
`RenderSessionHandle` have no runtime to be given one: after #399 a session is
built by `MapAttachRef`, which by design carries nothing but the map's address.
One hook per isolate covers them, because `mln_runtime_rebind_thread` re-homes
the runtime, its maps, its projections and every render session at once, under
the single-live-runtime assumption patch 0002 already documents.

How it goes away: Action 2 moves `render_update` onto the Choreographer thread,
after which either the engine isolate disappears entirely (nothing left to
migrate) or the four `HttpResourceProvider` awaits move off it (nothing left to
trigger migration). Either one retires this patch, and probably 0002 with it.

